{"name":"Bastille","hex":"#2c2c32","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Bastille","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A former fortress and prison in Paris, France, the storming of which in 1789 began the French Revolution."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Bastille"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bastille","blocks":[{"text":"The Bastille was a medieval fortress in Paris, known as the Bastille Saint-Antoine. It played an important role in the internal conflicts of France and for most of its history was used as a state prison by the kings of France. It was stormed by a crowd on 14 July 1789, in the French Revolution, becoming an important symbol for the French Republican movement. It was later demolished and replaced by the Place de la Bastille public square in Paris."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Bastille_Exterior_1790_or_1791.jpg/330px-Bastille_Exterior_1790_or_1791.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bastille","wikidata":"Q1865480"},{"title":"Bastille (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Bastille are an English indie pop band formed in 2010. The group began as a solo project by lead vocalist Dan Smith, but later expanded to include keyboardist Kyle Simmons, bassist and guitarist Will Farquarson and drummer Chris \"Woody\" Wood."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Bastille_lamav.JPG/330px-Bastille_lamav.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bastille_(band)","wikidata":"Q689"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Bastille_reconstruction_1420.jpg/500px-Bastille_reconstruction_1420.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Bastille_reconstruction_1420.jpg/1280px-Bastille_reconstruction_1420.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Bastille_reconstruction_1420.jpg/500px-Bastille_reconstruction_1420.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Historical reconstruction showing the moat below the walls of Paris (left), the Bastille and the Porte Saint-Antoine (right) in 1420","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABastille_reconstruction_1420.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Bastille_towers_profile.jpg/500px-Bastille_towers_profile.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Bastille_towers_profile.jpg/1280px-Bastille_towers_profile.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Bastille_towers_profile.jpg/500px-Bastille_towers_profile.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABastille_towers_profile.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Bastille_district_1575.jpg/500px-Bastille_district_1575.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Bastille_district_1575.jpg/500px-Bastille_district_1575.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A depiction of the Bastille and neighbouring Paris in 1575, showing the new bastions, the new Porte Saint-Antoine, the Arsenal complex and the open countryside beyond the city defences","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABastille_district_1575.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Callot_view_of_the_Bastille.jpg/500px-Callot_view_of_the_Bastille.jpg?utm_sourc